    sessionCounter = 0;
  }

  27. Date.now() and token generation aren't injectable, complicating deterministic tests (server.js:6, 29-30)
  Symptom: created: Date.now() and 'tok_' + sessionCounter are hard-coded calls with no way to control or mock them from
  a test without global monkey-patching (jest.spyOn(Date, 'now'), etc.).
  Why it matters: Testing time-sensitive behavior (e.g., a future session-expiry check, per finding #13) becomes fragile
  and coupled to global mutation of Date/crypto, rather than clean dependency injection.
  Fix: accept a clock/ID-generator as an optional parameter (or module-level, swappable dependency) so tests can supply
  deterministic fakes:
  export function addUser(n, e, a, { now = Date.now } = {}) {
    users.push({ n, e, a, created: now() });
    return users.length;
  }

  28. No test coverage accompanies this diff at all
  Symptom: The diff adds five new exported functions (login, getSession, listUsersByAge, exportAll, importAll) and
  modifies the behavior of existing ones, with zero corresponding test file changes.
  Why it matters: Given how many of the above bugs (off-by-one loop, eval RCE, predictable tokens, broken auth) are
  exactly the sort of thing a basic unit test (findUser returns undefined for a missing user; login rejects wrong
  passwords; importAll rejects non-JSON) would have caught before merge, the absence of tests is itself a significant
  gap for a diff touching authentication.
  Fix: add unit tests per function before merging, especially negative-path tests ("user not found", "wrong password",
  "malformed import payload").

  ---

  Given the presence of a remote-code-execution vector (eval in importAll), broken/non-functional authentication,
  predictable session tokens, and multiple correctness bugs that cause crashes or silent data corruption on common
  inputs, this diff should not be merged as-is.

  VERDICT: REVISE

